 "text": "Hi, how have you been? That's nice of her, but it' simple rental. Prices can really add up. Sure, take your time. So, and you want to try backpacking gear too? That adds a bit more. So, camping with gear, that's few nights at the very basic with a sleeping bag, or fewer days if you share the bag with someone. Renting includes a tent too, which is slower. Totally fair. If you change your mind and want to try backpacking, think of the time spent setting up and packing each time. Rental gear is still faster at the start.",
